//Stable pin (v0.12.1): a chained '<' comparison at a statement head
//still never compiles. The head '<' rides the type-argument reading
//(shift wins in the head states), the second '<' arms the nesting
//depth, the ">>" splits, and the statement parses as a declaration --
//the name resolver then rejects it: cannot resolve the type "a".
//Chained comparisons are also semantically illegal (bool
//comparisons are strict), so the shape has no legal spelling.
int main() {
    int a = 1;
    int b = 2;
    int c = 3;
    int d = 4;
    a < b < c >> d;
    return 0;
}
